Z||000000||Jake_Dragon||02-27-2001||09:42 PM||||I need some expert advice on what motor (engine) will fit in my car.<BR>It’s an 85-sport coupe 2.5-L automatic. I would like to find a low mileage 2.5 for a replacement and would like some tips on what would bolt in without any modifications.<BR>The current motor has over 100000 on it and is leaking from front and rear seals, it has very poor pickup and getting terrible gas mileage. It does have good oil pressure and is not knocking. I just don't have time to do a rebuild and will probably get the swap done somewhere. Any tips on keeping this as low budget as possible? Anyone ever deal with any mechanics from central Florida (Lakeland)? <BR>Thanks Jake.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jake_Dragon<BR>1985 2.5L Sport Coupe<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/rebel33/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000001||gabriel||02-27-2001||10:31 PM||||Hello Jake.  How are you doing over there in Lakeland?<P>&gt;I need some expert advice on what motor (engine) will fit in my car.<BR>It’s an 85-sport coupe 2.5-L automatic. I would like to find a low mileage 2.5 for a replacement and would like some tips on what would bolt in without any modifications.<P>I'm not sure what exactly you are asking, Jake.<P>Any Fiero motor, including the V-6, will bolt in, & a replacement 2.5 is an easy swap.<P>If you are asking about any GM motor, well that could be different - there are many engines that will bolt right up but there might be issues such as the ECM.<P>&gt;Any tips on keeping this as low budget as possible? Anyone ever deal with any mechanics from central Florida (Lakeland)? <BR>Thanks Jake. <P>Hehe.  Yah, do it yourself.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  There is plenty of support here on this Forum for any swap, right up to a SBC.<P> Use the search function & do it in the archives. - enter swap, 2.5, V-6, etc. for lots of info.<P> Please elaborate on your swap wishes.<P>   -g<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jake_Dragon||02-28-2001||06:22 AM||||I want to replace what I have with a low mileage 2.5, the idea of finding a low mileage fiero that is being parted out didn’t sound realistic so I would like some idea what would be a <B>good donor car</B>. I have a 1990 Buick with a 2.5 and I was just wondering what other GM had the same mounting points. I want to stay with the 2.5 because of the EMC.||||reg||3
